# Decision checkpoint before acquisition
Original endpoint: PMP22 regulatory system, separating promoter, RNA, translation, protein maturation and persistence. Inherited expression predictors failed and cannot be rescued by another retrospective correlation.

Candidate experiments:
* PMC5730339 chronic stress/ISR: potentially matched transcriptome/translatome with upstream ISRIB perturbation; non-Schwann cultured cells, so tests mechanism in that context only. Need inspect design, processed file availability, biological units and RNA/translation matching. Search excerpt already exposes PMP22 congruent regulation: target headline reproduction must be retrospective. Broad discordant RNA/translation and kinetics could reveal overlooked structure.
* PMC11370802 human iPSC-SCP dosage and lipidomics: human relevance, but donor/genotype and differentiation can confound; expression/lipid changes alone cannot isolate regulatory feedback. Published lipid suppression exposed by search.
* PMC10940316 PI3K/Akt/mTOR perturbation: directly tests upstream signaling in nerve; inspect molecular endpoints and source-data availability. Phenotypic rescue cannot itself identify PMP22 regulation.
* Existing co-IP data: intact artifacts but selected universe and missing replicate channels limit further mechanistic inference. No repeated selected-list ranking planned.

Choose metadata/full-text inspection of ISR and mTOR first because orthogonal endpoints distinguish transcriptional from translational mechanisms. Conditional on suitable processed measurements, prioritize matched RNA/translation analysis including broad feature universe, eligibility, perturbation interaction, biological replication and negative-control targets. No new prospective claim yet; freeze any independent prediction before outcome inspection. Reserve roughly half the 60-minute allowance for follow-up, robustness, novelty and preservation. New transport limits 150 requests/1GiB, inherited transport kept separate.
